# Summary: Pi artifact commands

Artifacts are files a pi session saves outside the git repo so they survive
across sessions (see `dotfiles/pi/.pi/agent/extensions/artifacts.ts`).

The filesystem is the source of truth:

    <tmpdir>/pi-artifacts/<hash>/
      <slug>.<ext>     the artifacts
      .index.json      optional sidecar with a title and type per file

`<hash>` is the first 16 hex characters of the sha256 of the project root (git
top-level, falling back to the given path). The sidecar only enriches a
listing; the set of artifacts is whatever non-dotfiles exist in the directory.

The directory lives under `$TMPDIR` and is cleared on reboot, so its absence is
normal and every command here treats it as an empty project.
